Whisper: the mark of the web on every saved file, without addresses

What: on Windows every file the browser saves gets a Zone.Identifier stream with
ZoneId=3 (Internet), also when the address maps to the local, intranet or trusted zone
and when the SaveZoneInformation policy is set; HostUrl and ReferrerUrl are never
written.
Why: the mark is what makes Windows (SmartScreen, Office's Protected View, script
hosts) treat a downloaded file as untrusted; Firefox skipped it for some zones and for
the policy, which malware sets to silence those warnings. The addresses in the mark are
a record on disk of where each file came from (research notes, logs_and_traces.md and
code_execution_defense.md: "метка без адреса"); Firefox already leaves them out in
private windows. Covers downloads and Save As (nsWebBrowserPersist).
